            <ArticleTitle>Accidental Intrathecal Administration of Digoxin in an Elderly Male with End-Stage Renal Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9072018</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/9072018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The systemic effects of digoxin toxicity have been well-known. However, there has been no case citing the effects of intrathecal digoxin in light of end-stage renal disease in the elderly. Here, we report on the case of the successful management of accidental intrathecal digoxin administration in an elderly male with end-stage renal disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
